{
  "_doc": "Safe-by-construction display-name POOLS for World Plaza (R2-6 Pair Identity). Names compose as `<Adjective> <Noun>` (+ optional 2-3 digit number) — the SAME construction across every pool. `pool-universal` is the FIXED, reviewed, language-neutral fallback (the original global list); the runtime falls back to it for any nameSeed id a per-language pool lacks, so a name NEVER becomes unreadable. Per-language pools (`pool-es`, `pool-ja`, `pool-zh`, …) SHARE ids with the universal pool where the concept maps 1:1 (so a persisted nameSeed {adjId,nounId} stays portable across pools) and only localize the WORD. Pools may be subsets. Every word in every pool is curated to the same bar: wholesome, global, non-identifying, NO real first/last names, no places, nothing edgy, kid-safe. NEVER freeform. The `id` is what GeneratedIdentity.nameSeed stores; `label` is the displayed word.",
